      "abstract": "Review of survodutide's hepatic mechanism of action. Glucagon receptor activation in liver drives enhanced lipid oxidation and anti-fibrotic effects. Explains superior MASH outcomes vs GLP-1-only agents."
    },
    {
      "id": "PMID:39156781",
      "type": "pubmed",
      "title": "Glucagon receptor agonism: therapeutic target for metabolic liver disease",
