      "abstract": "Review of glucagon's hepatic effects. The liver lacks GLP-1R but is rich in GCGR, explaining why dual agonists like survodutide may have advantages for liver disease over GLP-1-only agonists."
    },
    {
      "id": "PMID:38234119",
